# Reach a goal, avoid a risk in Russian: достичь цели, следовать плану
subtitle: "Достичь цели, избегать риска, следовать плану, доверять другу: four verbs that choose their own case — as Ольга reads Tom's business plan."
tags: ["russian","russian genitive","russian dative","verb government","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/verb-cases","vocabulary/money","vocabulary/business"]
thumb: "band \"Reach a goal, follow a plan — in Russian\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
